From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:23:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] util/ifdtool: Decode 4-bit component densities for the 8 and
 9 series

ifdtool takes the descriptors of the 8 and 9 series PCHs (Lynx Point,
Wildcat Point) for version 1, with 3-bit density fields in FLCOMP, but
these PCHs, like Wellsburg, use 4-bit fields: a W541 with an 8 MiB and
a 4 MiB chip (FLCOMP 0x34) was printed as 8 MB and 32 MB, and -D would
have set the density in the wrong bits.

Treat them as version 1.5: the regions of version 1, the densities of
version 2.

TEST=ifdtool -d on the W541 image prints 8MB and 4MB; nothing else in
the output changes.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 util/ifdtool/ifdtool.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/util/ifdtool/ifdtool.c b/util/ifdtool/ifdtool.c
index a3b66fd46..07bc4d8ff 100644
--- a/util/ifdtool/ifdtool.c
+++ b/util/ifdtool/ifdtool.c
@@ -337,6 +337,16 @@ static void check_ifd_version(char *image, int size)
 	} else {
 		ifd_version = IFD_VERSION_1;
 		chipset = ifd1_guess_chipset(image, size);
+		/*
+		 * The 8 and 9 series PCHs keep the regions of version 1 but,
+		 * like Wellsburg, encode the component densities in 4-bit
+		 * fields: a 0x34 of FLCOMP is 8 MiB and 4 MiB, not 8 and 32.
+		 */
+		if (chipset == CHIPSET_8_SERIES_LYNX_POINT ||
+		    chipset == CHIPSET_8_SERIES_LYNX_POINT_LP ||
+		    chipset == CHIPSET_9_SERIES_WILDCAT_POINT ||
+		    chipset == CHIPSET_9_SERIES_WILDCAT_POINT_LP)
+			ifd_version = IFD_VERSION_1_5;
 		max_regions = MIN(max_regions_from_fdbar(fdb), MAX_REGIONS_OLD);
 	}
 }
